From 1c61f3f079c9f8c777d7cfeca9c1b6daf0c58a5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Stoyan <andrey.stoyan.csam@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 14:14:58 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat(chexc): annotate stdx.encoding.json (28 -> 6)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

'JsonValue.toJsonString', 'toStringWithoutEscaping' and 'toJsonStringWithoutEscaping', the
'ToJson' interface's two members, the typed accessors of 'JsonValue' ('asInt', 'asObject', …),
'JsonValue.fromStr' and the two indexing operators declare 'JsonException' -- which every one of
them already documented with an '@throws' line.

What is left is six 'toString()' implementations that raise 'JsonException' over a clause-free
'std.core.ToString'. That is a ruling for the author, not a local fix (gap-analysis Q-STD-8): the
clause cannot be written where the failure happens, so either 'toString' stays clause-free and
these raise an unchecked exception, or 'ToString' declares a clause and every call site in the
language pays for it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
